Subject: hyper-transport's acknowledgement and erasure coding stated as before
Why: hyper-raft's main, merged with Mantle's line for kiln's one copy, adds Limits::acknowledgement (its docs/transport.md §4ak) and Limits::fec_window (§4an); a node's transport states them as every connection had them before: decimated acknowledgements, for its streams of data, and no erasure coding

diff --git a/crates/protocol/src/bounds.rs b/crates/protocol/src/bounds.rs
index e17157ddc24eca133a19a96e4b5ea846a7ebcc96..d9e359828c58fbc754b82c0f18f0c01d4b72b869 100644
--- a/crates/protocol/src/bounds.rs
+++ b/crates/protocol/src/bounds.rs
@@ -220,6 +220,12 @@ pub fn limits(stated: &Stated) -> Result<Limits, Unfit> {
         // pending places are taken (RFC 9000 §8.1.2), as before hyper-transport could count
         // the handshakes' bytes instead.
         retry_bytes: None,
+        // As every connection asked before hyper-transport let an endpoint choose (its
+        // docs/transport.md §4ak): a node's replication and a volume's chunks are streams of data
+        // whose congestion control waits on their acknowledgements.
+        acknowledgement: hyper_transport::Acknowledgement::Decimated,
+        // No forward erasure correction (§4an), as before it came.
+        fec_window: None,
     })
 }
 
